Z||000000||JBGehling||12-02-2000||11:49 PM||||Ok, I'm thinking about taking the big step and turbocharging my 88 GT. First of all, I need to know where to find a reliable kit for the car. Secondly, what would the cost be, approximately?<P>Josh||||reg||1
Z||000001||turbo86se||12-02-2000||11:56 PM||||Mine is a MillerWoods turbo, it's been in my 86SE for about eight years, with no problems, well, except for destroying the automatic transmission. Now I've got a new one in there, and no problems. The turbo system is very reliable, and responsive, it's always there when you need it. <P>Cost, about 5 grand installed at IRM.<BR>Not cheap, but worth every penny!!<P>You're not too far away for a test drive!||||reg||1
Z||000002||RedOktober||12-04-2000||02:15 AM||||Mine is a Miller Woods setup too. Got the turbo reclipped( to give me more boost). IHI turbo is expensive to replace, but gives good low end response.<P>go see design1( really cool guys), or call IRM(werent too much help for turbo details)<BR>Good Luck!<P>------------------<BR>86 SE V6 Auto Turbo Going 3.4 OHV "Red Oktober"<BR>86 2M4 5sp (Beater) "Blackie"<BR>87 GT "Blue Flame"||||reg||1
